NAME: ke2e-inject
LAST DEPLOYED: Thu May 28 20:24:33 2026
NAMESPACE: kubeclaw-e2e-injection
STATUS: deployed
REVISION: 1
TEST SUITE: None
NOTES:
KubeClaw has been deployed to namespace "kubeclaw-e2e-injection".

=== Next Step: Add a Channel ===

Open the admin shell to connect a messaging channel.

Exec (interactive terminal inside the pod):

  kubectl exec -it deployment/kubeclaw-orchestrator -n kubeclaw-e2e-injection -- node dist/admin-shell.js

HTTP browser UI — set these env vars in the orchestrator Deployment and expose via Service + Ingress:

  ADMIN_HTTP_PORT=9090
  ADMIN_HTTP_USERNAME=admin
  ADMIN_HTTP_PASSWORD=<your-password>

Tell it in plain English: "set up Telegram", "add Discord", etc.
It will ask for credentials, create the channel pod, and register your first group.

=== Status ===

  kubectl get pods -n kubeclaw-e2e-injection
  kubectl logs -f deployment/kubeclaw-orchestrator -n kubeclaw-e2e-injection

=== Tool Jobs ===

  kubectl get jobs -n kubeclaw-e2e-injection
  kubectl logs job/<job-name> -n kubeclaw-e2e-injection

